<section id="top">
        <div class="page-shell">
            <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
            <h1>Cookie Policy</h1>
            <p class="page-lede">This page explains how quickler.co uses cookies and local browser storage. The site is set up to avoid loading analytics unless you actively allow them.</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-tight">
        <div class="detail-shell">
            <div class="detail-body">
                <h3>What quickler uses now</h3>
                <p>Quickler currently uses a small browser-stored preference to remember whether you accepted or declined analytics cookies. If you decline, analytics scripts are not loaded.</p>

                <h3>Strictly necessary storage</h3>
                <p>The cookie consent tool stores your preference so the site can remember your choice. This is used only to operate the consent mechanism itself.</p>

                <h3>Analytics cookies</h3>
                <p>If you accept analytics, quickler uses Google Analytics to measure general website usage such as page views, referral sources, device/browser information, and rough location patterns. This helps improve the site and understand which pages are useful.</p>

                <h3>Google Fonts</h3>
                <p>The site loads its typeface (Space Grotesk) from Google Fonts on every page view. Google Fonts does not set cookies, but your browser connects directly to Google servers to fetch the font files, which means Google may receive your IP address and basic request headers. This happens before the analytics-consent prompt is answered because the font is needed to render the page. If you prefer to avoid this connection, most browsers can be configured to block third-party font requests.</p>

                <h3>Third-party services</h3>
                <p>Analytics and consent functions may rely on third-party services such as Google Analytics and the cookie-consent tooling used on the site. Those providers may set or read their own cookies in line with their service design.</p>

                <h3>Managing your choice</h3>
                <p>You can change your analytics choice at any time by using the cookie settings link in the footer. You can also control cookies through your browser settings.</p>

                <h3>Changes</h3>
                <p>This policy may be updated if the site's analytics, consent, or tracking setup changes.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
